{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/764428-so-a-beast-changeling-and-sin-eater-walk-into-a-bar","id":764428,"title":"So, a Beast, Changeling and Sin Eater walk into a bar...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-12T15:11:48-08:00","id":764428,"title":"So, a Beast, Changeling and Sin Eater walk into a bar...","content":"Well, perhaps not a bar, but for some reason I have in my head a game where a Beast, a Changeling and a Sin Eater are all living together in some capacity, forming a group and helping each other out while dealing with their respective foes together. Changeling 2e appears to have an option for allowing synergy with Sin Eaters, if you pardon the pun, by dealing with the dead and Beasts are practically built for crossovers.<br /> <br /> My question is, does this feel like it'd be too busy of a game? Too many aspects from the three gamelines not quite meshing together or being supported by one another? Beasts are able to bolster other supernaturals just as they can be empowered by them, but at the same time Sin Eaters and Changelings don't exactly have a lot of groundwork to go together with in terms of working together.<br /> <br /> I dunno, something about this mix from three different walks of life is interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T19:18:43-08:00","id":764626,"title":"","content":"Sin Eaters and Changelings may not have a lot of groundwork, but perhaps Chloe and Amber knew each other before Chloe was taken in the night by the Gentle Folk. Perhaps Amber was there when it happened, and died upon the Thorns as she tried to save her friend. Perhaps Amber subsequently returned to life as a Sin-Eater, realized that the thing pretending to be Chloe wasn't her, and went to a Beast for help to save her friend from the crazy faeries. Together, they go to the Hedge and find their way to Arcadia only to discover that Chloe was in the middle of organizing her own escape. Shenanigans ensue. The end result is that the three of them Escape from Arcadia, and now, as a Power Trio of Beast, Sin-Eater, and Changeling, together they fight crime. Or help the hopeless. Or possibly just try not to kill each other because living with roommates is hard.<br /> <br /> Alternately, maybe Jack and Michael are on the same community baseball team. Or maybe Susan and Maxine LARP together on weekends. Maybe Ken and Trevor and Jamie all meet up every Thursday to play board games at their FLGS. The point is, the individual lives of any character can provide a multitude of connections even where the supernatural world, by default, doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 11-12-2015, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T21:14:32-08:00","id":764706,"title":"","content":"That's a very fair point; I was more speaking in terms of GMing such a thing, the logistics of it all, but I suppose that's more up to the skill of the GM rather than anything else. It'd probably not be much harder than many other crossover games.<br /> <br /> Also, nice scenario ideas posted up there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T07:58:41-08:00","id":767070,"title":"","content":"Maybe I've missed it, but I'm curious where you saw the synergy option within 2e you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T14:18:02-08:00","id":767320,"title":"","content":"In the 75% complete version of the Changeling Kiths page, there's the Gravewright Kith, which gives a Changeling powers over ghosts (add or remove an Anchor, Open, Controlled or Materialized condition to or from a person, location or object), and removing conditions cannot be undone for a week save by the Changeling who caused them. They're also able to see, hear and speak to ghosts in the Twilight. I'm not entirely sure if that's still in the game though (I hope it is). Kinda figured that, even if a Changeling can't use the same powers/rituals as a Sin Eater, they can still be handy for handling ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T07:49:30-08:00","id":786721,"title":"","content":"Taking it from the other direction, there's a Tier 3 Krewe option that lets you create a new Key. If you go with the notion that there's a little known \u201cDead Conspiracy\u201d that featured an Astral Key, you could make Astral Space the thing that serves as a common bond between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:07:59-08:00","id":786802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/764428-so-a-beast-changeling-and-sin-eater-walk-into-a-bar?p=786721#post786721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking it from the other direction, there's a Tier 3 Krewe option that lets you create a new Key. If you go with the notion that there's a little known \u201cDead Conspiracy\u201d that featured an Astral Key, you could make Astral Space the thing that serves as a common bond between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd read about that on tvtropes actually, but only so far as Krewes being able to make a new Key. I assumed that it was the Stygian Key...in spite of the evidence it's a solo thing. Suddenly the Underbrush Key idea I had isn't so unlikely!<br /> <br /> But that is an interesting idea, crafting a Key that resonates with the other members, particularly Astral space. It may even provide a method of easier access to the Dead Dominion, where someone could access it by dreaming of it ... very interesting indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}